      "side": 0,
      "message": "I agree that we should remove the assert, but its presence was there to give a quicker/clearer error to something that may fail later.  In my quick look at the java code it seems to expect that the mUnitTests array is not null which this assert would have caught.\n\nNot crashing could be a side effect of how the JVM is implemented or it could be documented behavior that JNI is intended to return an empty array.  Just because it works now doesn\u0027t mean it won\u0027t cause a failure in the future (if you are relying on undefined behavior).\n\nThis CL may be valid for both cases, but it doesn\u0027t absolve us from doing due diligence when removing it. That extra check is to make sure we are not just postponing a problem to a future date.",
